{
  "about": [
    "Placements, read by two test suites: crates/pult-schema/tests/transforms.rs and",
    "frontend/src/lib/scene.test.ts. Composing a parent chain has to give the same",
    "answer on a station and in a browser — dragging a truss re-composes every child",
    "per frame and cannot be a round trip — and this file is what makes that a test",
    "rather than a promise. It lives outside both because neither owns it.",
    "",
    "`matrices` starts from a matrix as an MVR file writes one: four brace-wrapped",
    "rows of three, millimetres, X right, Y upstage, Z up. That is pult-mvr's half,",
    "and it is here so that the space conversion and the decomposition agree with",
    "what the console then does with the result.",
    "",
    "`chains` is the console's own half: a local placement, the objects above it, and",
    "where it therefore is. Angles are XYZ Euler degrees; a negative scale is a",
    "reflection, which is the only way to say that a drawing mirrored something."
  ],
